A||||9||fierohoho||Factory subwoofer install question!||||1||
Z||000000||fierohoho||12-03-2001||03:01 AM||||I will be installing a factory unit in my 1985 Coupe project car and right now I have the dash removed.<P>When I hold the sub up to the area where it should mount it seems the small block on the side of the heater housing that holds the chime box and flasher relay is in the way of the back sub-box projection.<P><BR>Soooooooooo......I have several questions.<P>What year was the factory sub first offered?<P>Has anyone done an install in the '85 and what mods did you have to do?<P>Would the heater housing be different between non-sub year cars and sub year cars, if so how?<P>I could post a couple pics of the area where it goes in my car or maybe someone has some they took when they did it.<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lightbar.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Haze_Performance||12-03-2001||03:27 AM||||Well. I put one in my '85.. The easy way is to get a heater core door/cover from a car that had a system. The hard way is to make your own brackets.. I went with a used junkyard door/cover. Its VERY easy to install everything, Top bolt into the heater core door bracket & the other into the bottom dash bolt. ..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlife.gif">       <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="red">1984 Indy For Sale ~ <A HREF="http://www.ClassicFiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> </FONT></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 12-03-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000002||mrfixit58||12-03-2001||08:27 AM||||I believe ALL 87-88 heater covers were made with the bracket you need.<P><P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>Suncoast Fieros<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <P><B>JUST ADDED: </B>1988 GT w/ T-Tops, 5-Speed, and Performance Sound.||||reg||6
Z||000003||Oreif||12-03-2001||09:48 AM||||The sub was offered from 1986 until 1988. <BR>You can change the cover with any 86-88.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierohoho||12-03-2001||10:59 AM||||Here's a couple pics of the cover difference.<P>Took the heater cover out of the '85...<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/85cover.jpg">  <P>Then took the heater cover out of th '86...<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/86cover.jpg">  <P>And swaped them so the Sub would fit...<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/subinplace.jpg">  <P>not bolted in yet but soon, thanks for all the help guys.<P><BR>[This message has been edited by fierohoho (edited 12-05-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by fierohoho (edited 12-05-2001).]||||reg||1
