Z||000006||jelly2m8||12-05-2001||06:29 PM||||Ahh yes, but what about non-AC equipped cars?<P> I asked this question before, but didnt get a reply.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||fierohoho||12-06-2001||06:29 AM||||I have a complete non-A/C heater setup from a '84 and I will post a pic of that heater cover for comparison but I think it is the same as the '85.<P>Hope to post the pic this afternoon.||||reg||1
Z||000008||fierohoho||12-06-2001||02:12 PM||||jelly2m8,<P>This first pic is the under dash view of my '84 with A/C. It's about the same as the '85<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/84_with_AC.jpg">  <P>These next two pics show a top view and right side view of the heater unit from a '84 non-A/C car.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/84_non_AC_top_view.jpg"> <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/84_non_ac.jpg"> <P>The right side view has the area where the courtesy center was mounted (circled in white) on a small metal mount, I have it somewhere but couldn't find it.<P>From what I can tell you could put a factory sub into your non A/C '84 as it seems to have enough room, but, you would have to fabricate a mount for the left side support comming off of the sub itself.<P>LMK if you need any other clarification pics.<p>[This message has been edited by fierohoho (edited 12-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||jelly2m8||12-06-2001||02:33 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierohoho:<BR><B>jelly2m8,<BR> From what I can tell you could put a factory sub into your non A/C '84 as it seems to have enough room, but, you would have to fabricate a mount for the left side support comming off of the sub itself.<P>[This message has been edited by fierohoho (edited 12-06-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thats exactly my question, maybe I didn't clarify it. Is there such a thing as a bracket to support the left side of the sub inclosure to the heater box on a non-AC equipped car?<P> I have only seen the sub option on airconditioned cars.<BR> <BR> Even the later year Fieros do not seem to have a tab, or bracket there on non-AC cars.<P> BTW AC equipped Fiero's are pretty few and far between around here, so I don't think that someone took the sub enclosures out of all these non-ac cars.<P> K, after all this, this is my question(s).<P> Was the sub system available from the factory on a non-AC equipped Fiero?<P> If so, does anybody have a picture of the left side mounting tab for the sub enclosure.<P> Thanks for you time and effort on the pics fierohoho<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> ||||reg||1
